                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "19922c0d-c935-32c5-b144-c2500090115b",
                        "entry_id": "3d68da7c-0829-3854-ac20-399141b46406",
                        "glosses": [
                            "fiktiver Ort oder fiktives Land mit einer idealen Gesellschaft"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1961058d-5f59-4f38-96b4-37a1a82e470c",
                                "sense_id": "19922c0d-c935-32c5-b144-c2500090115b",
                                "text": "Eine Weltkarte in der das Land Utopia nicht verzeichnet ist, verdient keine Beachtung, denn sie läßt die Küste aus, wo die Menschheit ewig landen wird."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2af04b25-1c96-4f36-8542-17c82727963e",
                                "sense_id": "19922c0d-c935-32c5-b144-c2500090115b",
                                "text": "\"Utopia. Was ist sie, die Gesellschaft der Zukunft? Wo ist das Ich, das Wir, das Abenteuer?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff5de2f5-eea7-490a-bd0e-f27b6e22c7b3",
                                "sense_id": "19922c0d-c935-32c5-b144-c2500090115b",
                                "text": "Vielleicht ist das Neue am Internet, dass es Utopie anders definiert. Seit Thomas Morus vor 500 Jahren seinen Roman Utopia veröffentlicht hat, verstehen wir unter Utopie einen Zukunftsentwurf für einen Staat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a10d6c2-443d-484b-950f-520ecb8b5aae",
                                "sense_id": "19922c0d-c935-32c5-b144-c2500090115b",
                                "text": "„Merry Mount ist aus der offiziellen Version der Geschichte getilgt worden, weil es kein Utopia der Tugend, sondern ein Utopia der Ehrlichkeit war.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "05f1d756-6fac-4613-80b8-28cfc3464b3e",
                        "source_entry_id": "3d68da7c-0829-3854-ac20-399141b46406",
                        "source_sense_id": "19922c0d-c935-32c5-b144-c2500090115b",
                        "source_sense_description": "fiktiver Ort oder fiktives Land mit einer idealen Gesellschaft",
                        "target_lang_word": "utopia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "utopia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                        "entry_id": "f381e887-13e1-34d3-aede-2675051ef4dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A world in which everything and everyone works in perfect harmony."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c19eb22-ace4-45f1-91a4-da6c5b28aae6",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "Errors in time must be kept in mind when analyzing myths and utopiae. Utopiae are merely projections, on a less personal and wider scale, of Cinderella’s longing for a happy future."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "788b304d-1305-4a6a-8140-91bd35a56b84",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "« Some peoples of Central or South Africa have conceived downright utopiae which enable them to build up a reality more tolerable than that in which they have to live daily »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21e9be19-9bd6-4660-bb30-b7ca4ee3e769",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "As everyone knows, almost all booked passenger and freight trains are diagrammed into rosters for engines and men, and in an operating Utopia everything would work out daily according to plan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf84947f-a63e-4ba8-b59f-3fea34f9ecb1",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "Efficiency for the sake of efficiency, unchallenged authority conferred upon those who know well a few things and ignore everything else, disdain for the ordinary and humble elements that introduce happiness in our lives, worship of unattainable utopiae, are some of the features of the scheme which leads inevitably to the suppression of the eternal gifts bestowed by God upon every human person and to the frightful prospect of being ruled by what he vividly names “the Empire of the Insect.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "787e97d3-2a72-40ec-99aa-0bf5c528969a",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "Orwell had correctly seen that the achievement of Wells’s ideas would be far from the frivolity of “Utopiae full of nude women” and visions of “super garden cities.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "739a9d46-5005-46c1-a211-168f267b2003",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "An interesting observation is that folk verses while talking of high standards of morality refer only to precedent generations and not to would-be utopiae, which in fact would rule out the possibility of evolution of a civilization absent before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4d01096-3ad0-4c76-8e47-1889389048ca",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "According to his model, palace and poetry function in tandem in order to communicate to an audience the ideas of utopiae of power, victory, eternity, and perfection. […] The ruins function, not as an evocation of past civilizations, but as the setting for the poet's dallying and revelry in youthful pleasures; his \"noble companions\" (probably Christians, given the reference to the length of their hair) are subjugated to the length of their pleasure, a reference to the \"stopping of time\", one of the utopiae out of which was constructed the licentious world of the khamriyya. […] I believe that these two utopiae are related to a profound consciousness, on the part of taifa royalty and courtiers, of the particular mutability of their reality: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8cf8b6a-cf0c-470c-ad54-5b18bc1050a8",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "So in order to conclude, how can we combine all these different aspects of the characteristic cross-relationship of negative and positive utopiae which are to be understood as counter projects to what there actually is?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96a6c217-9631-4065-ab67-f7259d569ed0",
                                                "sense_id": "2a34a359-e1f1-34e0-8163-10d17acd5d3b",
                                                "text": "As towns continue to grow, replanting vegetation has become a form of urban utopia and green roofs are spreading fast. Last year 1m square metres of plant-covered roofing was built in France, as much as in the US, and 10 times more than in Germany, the pioneer in this field."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
